{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
I [Am]am a poor wayfaring stranger,
While [Dm]trav'ling through this world of [Am]woe,
Yet there's no sickness, toil nor danger
In [Dm]that bright world [E7]to which I [Am]go.
I'm [Dm]going there to see my [Am]father,
I'm [Dm]going there no more to [E7]roam;
I'm [Am]only going over Jordan,
I'm [Dm]only going [E7]over [Am]home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
I [Am]know dark clouds will gather round me,
I [Dm]know my way is rough and [Am]steep;
Yet beauteous fields lie just before me,
Where [Dm]God's redeemed [E7]their vigils [Am]keep.
I'm [Dm]going there to see my [Am]mother,
She [Dm]said she'd meet me when I [E7]come;
I'm [Am]only going over Jordan,
I'm [Dm]only going [E7]over [Am]home.
{end_of_verse}
{x_end: Am}
